1
00:00:01,346 --> 00:00:02,506
Hey, are you listening to me?

2
00:00:03,429 --> 00:00:05,220
I told you!

3
00:00:05,304 --> 00:00:08,512
The auto-locking door
was left hanging wide open!

4
00:00:08,596 --> 00:00:09,716
Don't make me repeat myself!

5
00:00:11,262 --> 00:00:13,721
I already reported
this last week too!

6
00:00:13,804 --> 00:00:15,722
Why am I paying such
high management fees

7
00:00:15,805 --> 00:00:17,263
for such crappy service?

8
00:00:17,347 --> 00:00:18,388
Huh?

9
00:00:18,472 --> 00:00:19,388
What?

10
00:00:19,472 --> 00:00:21,180
Screw you, you'll do it today!

11
00:00:21,263 --> 00:00:22,303
Come inspect it right now!

12
00:00:23,430 --> 00:00:25,347
Are you even listening to me?

13
00:00:25,430 --> 00:00:27,097
You're dead!

14
00:00:31,972 --> 00:00:35,014
(opening theme music)

15
00:02:01,892 --> 00:02:04,808
Taichi Kanada in
Morioka, in June.

16
00:02:05,350 --> 00:02:08,850
Osamu Shimada in
Yokohama, in August.

17
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:12,892
Hiroshi Yamato in
Nagoya, in September.

18
00:02:14,224 --> 00:02:16,308
All three died in
similar circumstances.

19
00:02:18,224 --> 00:02:19,409
They were stabbed to
death by a cursed spirit

20
00:02:19,433 --> 00:02:22,683
at the entrances
to their apartments.

21
00:02:22,767 --> 00:02:25,517
And all three of them just
days prior to their murders

22
00:02:25,601 --> 00:02:29,142
had filed the same complaint
with their property managers.

23
00:02:29,225 --> 00:02:30,368
They all claimed they'd
found the security doors

24
00:02:30,392 --> 00:02:31,476
left wide open.

25
00:02:31,559 --> 00:02:34,060
"Episode 22: The Origin
of Blind Obedience"

26
00:02:34,142 --> 00:02:34,934
None of the other residents

27
00:02:35,018 --> 00:02:37,684
were able to provide
any other clues.

28
00:02:37,768 --> 00:02:39,410
But none of these
dates or locations match.

29
00:02:39,434 --> 00:02:42,642
Maybe it's not the
same cursed spirit?

30
00:02:42,726 --> 00:02:46,309
Hey wait, what if the spirit
is messing with the doors?

31
00:02:46,392 --> 00:02:49,184
Do cursed spirits trigger
those sensors, you think?

32
00:02:49,267 --> 00:02:51,101
They don't show up
on cameras, right?

33
00:02:51,976 --> 00:02:53,434
Apparently, the cursed spirit

34
00:02:53,517 --> 00:02:55,726
made the door operating
mechanism go crazy,

35
00:02:55,809 --> 00:02:56,809
not the sensors.

36
00:02:58,185 --> 00:02:59,268
Ohhh.

37
00:02:59,352 --> 00:03:01,518
Mechanisms?

38
00:03:01,602 --> 00:03:04,727
Yeah. And as for whether
or not the same cursed spirit

39
00:03:04,810 --> 00:03:05,894
was behind all three.

40
00:03:05,977 --> 00:03:09,185
We couldn't make a decision
based on the residuals.

41
00:03:09,268 --> 00:03:11,352
Too much time
had passed by then.

42
00:03:11,435 --> 00:03:15,061
So, we looked for connections
between the three of them.

43
00:03:15,143 --> 00:03:16,560
And we discovered that all three

44
00:03:16,643 --> 00:03:19,727
had attended the same
middle school for two years.

45
00:03:19,810 --> 00:03:21,185
Which would mean

46
00:03:21,268 --> 00:03:23,685
that all three must have
received the same curse.

47
00:03:23,769 --> 00:03:25,393
And it didn't activate
until years later?

48
00:03:25,477 --> 00:03:27,268
Oh!

49
00:03:27,352 --> 00:03:28,352
Precisely.

50
00:03:28,393 --> 00:03:29,560
That's highly likely.

51
00:03:29,643 --> 00:03:32,353
So that's why we're on our
way to their middle school now.

52
00:03:32,436 --> 00:03:35,394
We'll be picking up a fourth
man who also went there

53
00:03:35,478 --> 00:03:36,598
and knew all of the victims.

54
00:03:36,644 --> 00:03:39,103
I'm assigning you
three as sorcerers

55
00:03:39,186 --> 00:03:41,394
to see what you can
find out from him.

56
00:03:41,478 --> 00:03:43,311
Way to go, Kugisaki!

57
00:03:43,394 --> 00:03:45,269
Hah! No sweat.

58
00:03:46,478 --> 00:03:47,394
(sighs)

59
00:03:47,478 --> 00:03:49,561
"Spirit Lantern"

60
00:03:50,478 --> 00:03:52,478
"Morishita Family Funeral 11:00"

61
00:03:52,561 --> 00:03:53,603
[Itadori] A funeral?

62
00:03:54,853 --> 00:03:56,436
Is this the home of
that acquaintance?

63
00:03:56,519 --> 00:03:58,936
Yeah.

64
00:03:59,020 --> 00:04:00,186
Or it used to be.

65
00:04:01,811 --> 00:04:03,771
Well, this sucks.

66
00:04:03,854 --> 00:04:06,395
Turns out he died the
same way the other three did.

67
00:04:09,187 --> 00:04:11,507
He lived with his family, so
there was no auto-locking door,

68
00:04:11,562 --> 00:04:14,145
but he was killed
right at the entrance,

69
00:04:14,228 --> 00:04:15,645
just like the others.

70
00:04:15,729 --> 00:04:17,413
And he'd also recently told
other family members that

71
00:04:17,437 --> 00:04:19,354
another time he'd
come home alone,

72
00:04:19,437 --> 00:04:22,187
he'd found that "the
door was unlocked,

73
00:04:22,270 --> 00:04:23,270
"but it wouldn't open."

74
00:04:26,604 --> 00:04:29,145
I asked his parents about
the other three victims,

75
00:04:29,228 --> 00:04:31,039
but they said they didn't
know what relationship

76
00:04:31,063 --> 00:04:32,645
he might've had with them.

77
00:04:32,729 --> 00:04:34,354
Man, there goes our only lead!

78
00:04:34,437 --> 00:04:35,480
Aagh, don't worry!

79
00:04:35,563 --> 00:04:38,438
I'm sure we'll find something
at the middle school!

80
00:04:38,521 --> 00:04:40,980
I sure hope so.

81
00:04:41,064 --> 00:04:42,497
I've made you guys an
appointment with a teacher,

82
00:04:42,521 --> 00:04:45,022
so I'm counting on you.

83
00:04:45,105 --> 00:04:45,480
[Itadori] Roger that.

84
00:04:45,563 --> 00:04:47,563
Oh? (snicker)

85
00:04:48,438 --> 00:04:50,980
Hey, check out these two punks!

86
00:04:51,064 --> 00:04:52,813
How about we kick their asses?

87
00:04:52,897 --> 00:04:53,897
[Itadori] What for?

88
00:04:53,938 --> 00:04:54,855
Hmm?

89
00:04:54,938 --> 00:04:55,938
Huh?

90
00:04:57,105 --> 00:04:58,105
Hmmm?

91
00:05:00,396 --> 00:05:02,813
Uhh, it's good to see you again!

92
00:05:02,897 --> 00:05:03,521
Well, look at that.

93
00:05:03,605 --> 00:05:05,396
You're getting some respect.

94
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:08,023
An aura just pours out,

95
00:05:08,106 --> 00:05:09,814
even if you try
your best to hide it.

96
00:05:09,898 --> 00:05:12,439
[Student A] We haven't seen
you since graduation, Fushiguro!

97
00:05:14,939 --> 00:05:15,939
Huh?

98
00:05:17,939 --> 00:05:20,856
I uh went to school here.

99
00:05:20,939 --> 00:05:23,647
Well that's a surprise
but that's not the point!

100
00:05:23,731 --> 00:05:24,814
Explain yourself!

101
00:05:24,898 --> 00:05:25,814
What'd you do?

102
00:05:25,898 --> 00:05:27,689
What happened when
you were at this school?

103
00:05:27,773 --> 00:05:29,856
Wait! Maybe we should
just ask these two!

104
00:05:29,939 --> 00:05:32,481
Hey, Idiot A and Idiot B, just
what'd this guy do to you?

105
00:05:32,564 --> 00:05:36,230
We both, along with
every other stoner

106
00:05:36,314 --> 00:05:38,522
and slacker and delinquent
here at this school

107
00:05:38,606 --> 00:05:40,899
got beat up by Fushiguro.

108
00:05:40,982 --> 00:05:41,982
Huh?

109
00:05:46,774 --> 00:05:48,273
Pretty much, yeah.

110
00:05:48,774 --> 00:05:50,607
Why're you talking like a robot?

111
00:05:50,690 --> 00:05:51,899
Would you look at me!

112
00:05:51,982 --> 00:05:53,107
What is your deal?

113
00:05:53,190 --> 00:05:55,107
What the hell's going
on here with you?

114
00:05:55,190 --> 00:05:56,732
Hey you three!

115
00:05:56,815 --> 00:05:57,899
Who are you?

116
00:05:57,982 --> 00:05:59,750
Students from other schools
are not allowed in here!

117
00:05:59,774 --> 00:06:02,899
Who're you to be
questioning us, huh?

118
00:06:02,982 --> 00:06:03,565
He's clearly staff.

119
00:06:03,648 --> 00:06:06,066
Take it down a notch.

120
00:06:06,148 --> 00:06:07,565
We have permission
to visit today.

121
00:06:07,648 --> 00:06:08,565
Hmm?

122
00:06:08,648 --> 00:06:10,440
Ahh, the investigators?

123
00:06:10,523 --> 00:06:12,524
How very young you all are!

124
00:06:12,608 --> 00:06:15,608
Please keep your pass
visible for your entire stay here.

125
00:06:15,691 --> 00:06:17,900
Oh!

126
00:06:17,983 --> 00:06:19,149
Is that Fushiguro?

127
00:06:20,649 --> 00:06:21,900
Hello.

128
00:06:21,983 --> 00:06:23,941
[Both] He remembers you!

129
00:06:24,025 --> 00:06:26,733
So this man has been
here for a long time then?

130
00:06:26,816 --> 00:06:28,149
Probably.

131
00:06:28,232 --> 00:06:29,524
Takeda was a
member of the staff.

132
00:06:29,608 --> 00:06:31,608
Great, then I leave it to you!

133
00:06:31,691 --> 00:06:33,524
How convenient.

134
00:06:35,191 --> 00:06:39,566
Kanada, Shimada, Yamato
and now Morishita too, eh?

135
00:06:41,191 --> 00:06:43,399
It's quite a shock
to hear about this.

136
00:06:43,483 --> 00:06:45,400
But it must be
nearly 20 years now

137
00:06:45,484 --> 00:06:47,192
since those boys graduated.

138
00:06:48,484 --> 00:06:50,692
Still I remember it
like it was yesterday.

139
00:06:52,026 --> 00:06:54,400
They were all
problem children too,

140
00:06:54,484 --> 00:06:56,275
though not as bad as you.

141
00:06:56,359 --> 00:06:58,192
What do you want to know?

142
00:06:58,275 --> 00:06:59,650
Curious rumors, or dark rumors,

143
00:06:59,734 --> 00:07:02,442
or connections to bad adults.

144
00:07:02,525 --> 00:07:04,692
[Both] Hey, problem child!

145
00:07:04,776 --> 00:07:08,192
Also anything of
ill omen, of course.

146
00:07:08,275 --> 00:07:09,275
Dark rumors?

147
00:07:10,068 --> 00:07:11,068
They could be difficult,

148
00:07:11,150 --> 00:07:14,942
but it was just your
average middle school stuff.

149
00:07:15,026 --> 00:07:16,526
Then again, ill omen?

150
00:07:16,610 --> 00:07:18,651
Are you talking
about that old story?

151
00:07:18,735 --> 00:07:20,818
The Yasohachi Bridge?

152
00:07:20,902 --> 00:07:22,318
That one?

153
00:07:22,401 --> 00:07:24,193
You're still here A and B?

154
00:07:24,276 --> 00:07:26,234
What's the Yasohachi Bridge?

155
00:07:26,318 --> 00:07:27,777
It's a suicide site.

156
00:07:27,860 --> 00:07:30,818
Considered haunted
by some of the locals.

157
00:07:30,902 --> 00:07:32,443
Oh yes you're right!

158
00:07:32,526 --> 00:07:34,526
Back then it was all the
rage among delinquents

159
00:07:34,610 --> 00:07:37,360
to bungee jump off
Yasohachi Bridge late at night

160
00:07:37,443 --> 00:07:37,943
to test one's courage.

161
00:07:38,027 --> 00:07:40,193
What a bunch of weirdos.

162
00:07:40,276 --> 00:07:42,818
I'm surprised there are
people dumber than me!

163
00:07:42,902 --> 00:07:43,693
What do you use for a cord?

164
00:07:43,777 --> 00:07:45,693
No no, we don't bungee jump!

165
00:07:45,777 --> 00:07:47,735
We just heard people
talking about it.

166
00:07:47,818 --> 00:07:49,652
It's a thing from
back in the day.

167
00:07:49,736 --> 00:07:52,361
One day Kanada
and the other three

168
00:07:52,444 --> 00:07:54,235
all were absent
without permission.

169
00:07:54,319 --> 00:07:56,277
By itself that wasn't strange.

170
00:07:57,319 --> 00:07:59,861
Then, when we contacted
all of their families,

171
00:07:59,944 --> 00:08:01,819
we learned that
none of the four boys

172
00:08:01,903 --> 00:08:03,861
had come home from
school the day before.

173
00:08:05,652 --> 00:08:07,694
It caused a pretty big stir.

174
00:08:07,778 --> 00:08:11,986
Then they were found laying
under the bridge, unconscious.

175
00:08:12,070 --> 00:08:14,652
They got chewed
out good as I recall.

176
00:08:14,736 --> 00:08:17,361
But all four of them
swore up and down

177
00:08:17,444 --> 00:08:19,277
that they didn't
remember a thing.

178
00:08:21,320 --> 00:08:23,236
I think that's it.

179
00:08:23,320 --> 00:08:26,029
As a matter of fact
I've been to that bridge.

180
00:08:26,112 --> 00:08:27,112
To bungee jump?

181
00:08:27,737 --> 00:08:30,071
Just like in schools,

182
00:08:30,153 --> 00:08:33,320
curses can take root
in haunted locations.

183
00:08:33,403 --> 00:08:36,445
So people from Jujutsu High
regularly patrol that bridge.

184
00:08:37,362 --> 00:08:39,695
There wasn't anything
strange at the time.

185
00:08:39,779 --> 00:08:41,779
Even though it
became a little famous,

186
00:08:41,862 --> 00:08:44,236
it's still in use as
a normal bridge.

187
00:08:44,320 --> 00:08:46,570
We still have to go
and check it out though.

188
00:08:46,945 --> 00:08:48,278
I agree.

189
00:08:48,362 --> 00:08:49,362
Fushiguro?

190
00:08:50,362 --> 00:08:52,779
There's something I was
hoping to ask you about.

191
00:08:52,862 --> 00:08:53,780
What is it?

192
00:08:53,863 --> 00:08:56,072
When you were in school here

193
00:08:56,154 --> 00:08:58,613
Tsukimi always took care of you.

194
00:08:58,696 --> 00:09:01,030
Is she doing okay these days?

195
00:09:03,196 --> 00:09:04,363
Yes.

196
00:09:04,446 --> 00:09:05,780
Wait, who is Tsumiki?

197
00:09:05,863 --> 00:09:06,780
My sister.

198
00:09:06,863 --> 00:09:07,863
What?

199
00:09:07,946 --> 00:09:11,279
How come you never tell
us anything about yourself?

200
00:09:11,363 --> 00:09:12,863
Yeah, what she said!

201
00:09:14,404 --> 00:09:16,905
When they find cursed
objects like these...

202
00:09:16,988 --> 00:09:19,821
Why don't they
just destroy them?

203
00:09:19,905 --> 00:09:20,654
They can't destroy them.

204
00:09:20,738 --> 00:09:23,738
Not with the special-grades.

205
00:09:23,821 --> 00:09:25,780
So they use a pact to
put their life on pause

206
00:09:25,863 --> 00:09:30,322
to not harm others but
preserve their existence.

207
00:09:30,405 --> 00:09:32,697
[Mahito] Sukuna's
fingers still cause harm.

208
00:09:32,781 --> 00:09:34,655
That's an exception.

209
00:09:34,739 --> 00:09:38,114
Sukuna's a monster
that will still attract curses,

210
00:09:38,197 --> 00:09:39,947
even after it became
a cursed object

211
00:09:40,031 --> 00:09:41,781
and was divided into 20 pieces.

212
00:09:41,864 --> 00:09:44,906
So it can choose,
its own vessel.

213
00:09:45,864 --> 00:09:50,364
Huh, well, then anyone will
work for this purpose, right?

214
00:09:51,697 --> 00:09:52,697
(heaving breaths)

215
00:09:52,781 --> 00:09:54,697
Hey listen...

216
00:09:54,781 --> 00:09:56,697
Cash?

217
00:09:56,781 --> 00:09:57,781
Cash!

218
00:09:57,822 --> 00:09:59,008
Right? That's what
you want isn't it?

219
00:09:59,032 --> 00:10:00,990
I can get it!

220
00:10:01,074 --> 00:10:02,074
All you want!

221
00:10:03,406 --> 00:10:05,531
So will this one work okay?

222
00:10:05,615 --> 00:10:08,365
He still can't see me
even at this juncture.

223
00:10:08,448 --> 00:10:10,573
His ability level is low.

224
00:10:10,656 --> 00:10:11,990
Open up and say ahh!

225
00:10:12,074 --> 00:10:14,198
(gagging)

226
00:10:19,406 --> 00:10:21,365
(upbeat music)

227
00:10:21,448 --> 00:10:22,448
"Jujutsu Kaisen"

228
00:10:23,907 --> 00:10:26,823
(erie music)

229
00:10:26,907 --> 00:10:29,198
"Jujutsu Kaisen"

230
00:10:29,281 --> 00:10:34,199
(cars passing)

231
00:10:41,908 --> 00:10:43,157
[Akari] We're here.

232
00:10:43,240 --> 00:10:46,157
Koi no Kuchi Canyon,
Yasohachi Bridge.

233
00:10:46,240 --> 00:10:49,407
Once you confirm a cursed
spirit is here, I'll lower a veil.

234
00:10:50,616 --> 00:10:51,616
You got it!

235
00:10:51,949 --> 00:10:52,991
(erie music)

236
00:10:53,075 --> 00:10:56,908
Hey. Sorry to ask you
this when you just woke up.

237
00:10:56,991 --> 00:11:00,199
But could you go run
a little errand for me?

238
00:11:02,240 --> 00:11:03,742
(monster howl)

239
00:11:06,492 --> 00:11:07,825
(yawning)

240
00:11:10,784 --> 00:11:11,950
What a bust.

241
00:11:12,034 --> 00:11:13,867
Not hide nor hair
of a cursed spirit.

242
00:11:14,867 --> 00:11:20,076
We didn't sense any
presences or any residuals either.

243
00:11:20,158 --> 00:11:21,241
I see.

244
00:11:21,325 --> 00:11:22,034
I guess this isn't it.

245
00:11:22,117 --> 00:11:24,450
We're back to square one.

246
00:11:24,533 --> 00:11:25,926
Won't matters get
worse if we don't hurry?

247
00:11:25,950 --> 00:11:27,784
[Nobara] Why?

248
00:11:27,867 --> 00:11:30,867
Well it's a famous
haunted location, right?

249
00:11:30,950 --> 00:11:33,909
So, there might still be plenty
of others who got cursed.

250
00:11:33,992 --> 00:11:37,701
And right now, the death
rate's at a hundred percent.

251
00:11:37,785 --> 00:11:39,465
We don't want to see
any others die, right?

252
00:11:39,910 --> 00:11:42,077
[Nobara] Yeah, true.

253
00:11:42,159 --> 00:11:43,409
Donngg!

254
00:11:43,493 --> 00:11:45,576
Bungee jumping was
all the rage back then!

255
00:11:45,659 --> 00:11:48,409
So maybe the act of
jumping off is the key?

256
00:11:48,493 --> 00:11:49,077
Did she really just say "dong"?

257
00:11:49,201 --> 00:11:51,077
Did I actually hear that?

258
00:11:51,159 --> 00:11:52,077
She did, she did!

259
00:11:52,159 --> 00:11:55,451
Doesn't matter, Itadori
already tried that.

260
00:11:55,534 --> 00:11:56,534
Huh?

261
00:11:58,118 --> 00:11:59,284
Aagh!

262
00:11:59,368 --> 00:12:02,201
You didn't really jump with that
vinyl cord tied to you did you?

263
00:12:03,910 --> 00:12:04,826
Gyaaah!

264
00:12:04,910 --> 00:12:05,910
Agh!

265
00:12:07,576 --> 00:12:09,078
Hey, there you are!

266
00:12:09,160 --> 00:12:10,494
-Oh thank goodness!
-Hm?

267
00:12:10,577 --> 00:12:11,577
Fushiguro!

268
00:12:12,160 --> 00:12:14,078
Who's this guy?

269
00:12:14,160 --> 00:12:16,202
He's that guy you
were making fun of.

270
00:12:16,285 --> 00:12:17,078
I think you called
him "Idiot A".

271
00:12:17,160 --> 00:12:18,994
Oh!

272
00:12:19,078 --> 00:12:20,911
You were talking
about Yasohachi Bridge.

273
00:12:20,994 --> 00:12:23,078
So I thought I
might find you here.

274
00:12:23,160 --> 00:12:24,911
Fujinuma?

275
00:12:24,994 --> 00:12:26,078
Hm?

276
00:12:26,160 --> 00:12:27,619
A classmate.

277
00:12:27,702 --> 00:12:28,702
My big sister

278
00:12:30,577 --> 00:12:33,702
It's nice that you still
remember me, Fushiguro.

279
00:12:33,786 --> 00:12:35,928
[Idiot A] I was talking to
my sister about you yesterday

280
00:12:35,952 --> 00:12:37,494
and... uh...

281
00:12:38,119 --> 00:12:40,285
Yes well, Morishita's funeral

282
00:12:40,370 --> 00:12:41,530
was held in our neighborhood.

283
00:12:43,620 --> 00:12:45,328
So then when my brother said

284
00:12:45,411 --> 00:12:48,120
that you were looking into
him and also Yasohachi Bridge,

285
00:12:48,203 --> 00:12:51,912
I thought maybe the
two things were related.

286
00:12:55,244 --> 00:12:56,787
What two things?

287
00:12:56,870 --> 00:12:58,387
[Fujinuma] Morishita's
unexpected death,

288
00:12:58,411 --> 00:13:00,120
and Yasohachi Bridge.

289
00:13:00,203 --> 00:13:01,286
No they're not.

290
00:13:01,370 --> 00:13:02,286
No connection.

291
00:13:02,370 --> 00:13:03,703
You see, I...

292
00:13:03,787 --> 00:13:05,161
I went there too!

293
00:13:05,244 --> 00:13:08,161
In eighth grade I went to
the bridge late one night!

294
00:13:10,079 --> 00:13:12,536
Has anything out of the ordinary

295
00:13:12,620 --> 00:13:14,329
happened at home recently?

296
00:13:14,412 --> 00:13:16,056
Any strange feelings that
seem to only affect you

297
00:13:16,080 --> 00:13:17,080
and no one else?

298
00:13:21,204 --> 00:13:22,329
That's just it!

299
00:13:22,412 --> 00:13:24,829
You see my family runs
a shop here in town.

300
00:13:25,913 --> 00:13:27,204
And lately I've been finding

301
00:13:27,287 --> 00:13:30,080
the shop's automatic door
wide open when I come home,

302
00:13:30,162 --> 00:13:31,913
but it only happens to me!

303
00:13:32,954 --> 00:13:37,080
Mom and Dad both told
me it's just a coincidence.

304
00:13:37,162 --> 00:13:38,954
But there was definitely
something there!

305
00:13:40,121 --> 00:13:42,704
It scared me.

306
00:13:42,788 --> 00:13:46,747
And yesterday my brother
told me about you three

307
00:13:46,830 --> 00:13:49,997
and I remembered that
night out at the bridge.

308
00:13:50,081 --> 00:13:53,163
[Akari] When did the issue
with your automatic door start?

309
00:13:53,246 --> 00:13:54,264
[Fujinuma] It's happened
about every other day

310
00:13:54,288 --> 00:13:56,955
for exactly one week now.

311
00:13:57,039 --> 00:13:58,747
So there's at least two weeks

312
00:13:58,830 --> 00:14:00,580
between the time
when the four victims

313
00:14:00,663 --> 00:14:03,039
first noticed something
wrong and the day they died.

314
00:14:04,122 --> 00:14:05,747
We still have some time.

315
00:14:05,830 --> 00:14:07,872
Wait, you didn't go
out to that bridge

316
00:14:07,955 --> 00:14:09,122
all by yourself did you?

317
00:14:09,205 --> 00:14:10,306
Do you remember
who you went with?

318
00:14:10,330 --> 00:14:14,039
So then this really does
have something to do with--

319
00:14:14,122 --> 00:14:15,663
No it's just about your door!

320
00:14:15,747 --> 00:14:17,873
And it has nothing to
do with Morishita's death

321
00:14:17,956 --> 00:14:19,123
or anyone else's!

322
00:14:19,206 --> 00:14:20,790
Fushiguro and his friends here

323
00:14:20,873 --> 00:14:23,748
are just helping me with
research for my college report:

324
00:14:23,831 --> 00:14:25,140
"Electromagnetic Waves
from Haunted Locations

325
00:14:25,164 --> 00:14:27,873
"and their Effects
on Electronic Stuff

326
00:14:27,956 --> 00:14:29,664
Such a pain in the neck!

327
00:14:29,748 --> 00:14:32,414
But I need to get reports
from all kinds of sources.

328
00:14:32,498 --> 00:14:35,623
So I'd love to hear who was
with you out at the bridge.

329
00:14:35,706 --> 00:14:38,289
After lying to her like
this we'd better save her

330
00:14:41,498 --> 00:14:45,414
It was a test of courage for
three of us in the same club.

331
00:14:45,498 --> 00:14:46,498
And in fact, Fushiguro,

332
00:14:46,581 --> 00:14:49,414
your sister Tsumiki was
there with us that night.

333
00:14:50,874 --> 00:14:51,248
Tsumiki?

334
00:14:51,332 --> 00:14:53,083
Not his sister?

335
00:14:55,165 --> 00:14:56,415
I see.

336
00:14:56,499 --> 00:14:58,183
I'll ask Tsumiki what
she remembers about it.

337
00:14:58,207 --> 00:14:59,290
Okay!

338
00:14:59,374 --> 00:15:02,916
Then I guess I can just give
these two a ride back home now.

339
00:15:02,999 --> 00:15:05,457
You three keep working
on the report until I get back.

340
00:15:05,540 --> 00:15:07,415
There's something
going on here isn't there?

341
00:15:07,499 --> 00:15:10,582
Well I can't very well let you
both go home on one bike!

342
00:15:18,957 --> 00:15:19,957
Fushiguro.

343
00:15:21,540 --> 00:15:22,541
Fushiguro!

344
00:15:24,583 --> 00:15:26,958
Fushiguro, you've
gotta snap out of it.

345
00:15:27,042 --> 00:15:28,750
You gotta make
sure that she's safe!

346
00:15:32,541 --> 00:15:34,042
I'm alright.

347
00:15:34,125 --> 00:15:36,042
Hang on, I just need a moment.

348
00:15:43,375 --> 00:15:45,458
Yes, I understand.

349
00:15:45,541 --> 00:15:47,042
You need guard
for Tsumiki, right?

350
00:15:47,125 --> 00:15:50,125
I'll try, but as
far as sorcerers,

351
00:15:50,208 --> 00:15:52,833
second-grades are
all that's available.

352
00:15:52,917 --> 00:15:54,000
Second grade...

353
00:15:54,084 --> 00:15:55,365
And, since the number of victims

354
00:15:55,417 --> 00:15:57,501
there far exceeds our estimates,

355
00:15:57,584 --> 00:15:58,904
we'll probably
have to re-evaluate

356
00:15:58,959 --> 00:16:00,376
the curse's grade, as well.

357
00:16:02,584 --> 00:16:03,876
And another thing.

358
00:16:03,959 --> 00:16:05,310
You were probably
assigned this mission

359
00:16:05,334 --> 00:16:07,876
with Itadori's growth
taken into account.

360
00:16:07,959 --> 00:16:10,709
So if it's even more dangerous
than was originally thought,

361
00:16:10,793 --> 00:16:13,167
then it might be too much
for a second-grade sorcerer.

362
00:16:13,250 --> 00:16:16,542
It's just as dangerous
for all of you, as well.

363
00:16:16,626 --> 00:16:19,085
Personally, I recommend
you withdraw.

364
00:16:20,626 --> 00:16:21,626
What do I do?

365
00:16:22,751 --> 00:16:24,584
Do I go back by
myself right now?

366
00:16:25,167 --> 00:16:29,377
No, the mission was already
dangerous for all three of us.

367
00:16:29,460 --> 00:16:31,877
I can't leave it to
just the two of them.

368
00:16:31,960 --> 00:16:33,335
Gojo will return next week.

369
00:16:34,251 --> 00:16:35,531
I could wait and ask him then...

370
00:16:36,293 --> 00:16:38,710
No, I can't!

371
00:16:38,794 --> 00:16:40,710
The time limit is
the big problem!

372
00:16:40,794 --> 00:16:43,127
This isn't the type of cursed
spirit that attacks someone.

373
00:16:43,210 --> 00:16:45,293
It's the type that activates
a cursed technique

374
00:16:45,377 --> 00:16:46,502
from within a marked person.

375
00:16:46,585 --> 00:16:49,752
So there's no point staying
nearby and protecting them!

376
00:16:49,835 --> 00:16:51,752
I have to exorcise
it right away!

377
00:16:51,835 --> 00:16:54,044
Why were you talking
to Ijichi just now?

378
00:16:54,127 --> 00:16:54,418
About your sister?

379
00:16:54,502 --> 00:16:56,251
Is she okay?

380
00:16:56,335 --> 00:16:58,919
Yes she's fine.

381
00:16:59,002 --> 00:17:01,586
But this mission's
danger level just shot up.

382
00:17:01,669 --> 00:17:03,961
Other sorcerers will
be taking over the case.

383
00:17:04,628 --> 00:17:05,628
You two can go home now.

384
00:17:08,294 --> 00:17:10,419
Wait, why just us two?

385
00:17:10,503 --> 00:17:11,419
Hey!

386
00:17:11,503 --> 00:17:12,419
What about you?

387
00:17:12,503 --> 00:17:14,419
I'll leave after I say
goodbye to Takeda.

388
00:17:14,503 --> 00:17:16,128
Now just go!

389
00:17:23,252 --> 00:17:26,169
(cellphone rings)

390
00:17:26,252 --> 00:17:27,336
Hello, Nitta.

391
00:17:27,419 --> 00:17:29,586
Thanks for your help.

392
00:17:29,669 --> 00:17:31,796
There's something
I want to ask you.

393
00:17:31,879 --> 00:17:34,170
[Nitta] About the
procedure, right?

394
00:17:34,253 --> 00:17:37,337
Fujinuma didn't go over
the side of Yasohachi Bridge.

395
00:17:37,420 --> 00:17:39,540
They held their test of
courage underneath the bridge.

396
00:17:41,504 --> 00:17:43,420
Itadori went under it, too.

397
00:17:43,504 --> 00:17:46,420
[Nitta] Most likely, you can't
get below it from up above.

398
00:17:46,504 --> 00:17:49,253
The cursed spirit
is within its barrier,

399
00:17:49,337 --> 00:17:50,170
so the procedure's important.

400
00:17:50,253 --> 00:17:52,420
You go at night,
from underneath.

401
00:17:52,504 --> 00:17:54,587
And one more thing...

402
00:17:55,712 --> 00:17:57,271
It's impossible to
constantly keep a domain

403
00:17:57,295 --> 00:18:00,796
imbued with a technique
deployed forever.

404
00:18:02,046 --> 00:18:03,462
Which means it's
like that barrier

405
00:18:03,545 --> 00:18:06,130
at the juvenile
detention center,

406
00:18:06,213 --> 00:18:07,671
an incomplete domain.

407
00:18:09,171 --> 00:18:10,838
I'm actually lucky
this time around.

408
00:18:11,338 --> 00:18:13,838
Since I won't need a veil.

409
00:18:18,130 --> 00:18:19,522
You really don't tell us
enough about yourself.

410
00:18:19,546 --> 00:18:21,213
Sure don't.

411
00:18:23,713 --> 00:18:25,296
If you didn't
notice us until now

412
00:18:25,380 --> 00:18:27,505
you're seriously lost in space.

413
00:18:27,588 --> 00:18:29,356
We're not saying you
have to tell us everything

414
00:18:29,380 --> 00:18:31,671
but come on, at
least let us help.

415
00:18:32,546 --> 00:18:34,505
We're friends, aren't we?

416
00:18:43,381 --> 00:18:44,381
Tsumiki...

417
00:18:47,506 --> 00:18:48,422
Is still bedridden.

418
00:18:48,506 --> 00:18:49,506
(light gasps)

419
00:18:50,589 --> 00:18:52,339
The curse of the
Yasohachi Bridge

420
00:18:53,422 --> 00:18:55,464
only appears to its victims.

421
00:18:58,798 --> 00:19:00,506
Since she can't
communicate herself.

422
00:19:01,464 --> 00:19:04,297
I have no idea when
she'll be killed by the curse.

423
00:19:05,422 --> 00:19:07,255
So I want to
exorcise it right away.

424
00:19:09,173 --> 00:19:11,757
But now that our mission's
danger level increased...

425
00:19:12,799 --> 00:19:13,882
Okay, okay!

426
00:19:13,965 --> 00:19:15,340
Geez, we get it now.

427
00:19:15,423 --> 00:19:18,256
You should have just told
us all of that from the start.

428
00:19:22,007 --> 00:19:23,924
(pleased soft chuckle)

429
00:19:24,007 --> 00:19:26,049
The cursed spirit
is within its barrier,

430
00:19:26,132 --> 00:19:28,215
so the procedure's important.

431
00:19:28,298 --> 00:19:30,465
You go at night,
from underneath.

432
00:19:30,548 --> 00:19:32,007
And one more thing...

433
00:19:32,632 --> 00:19:35,423
At the bottom of the
canyon there might be a river.

434
00:19:42,257 --> 00:19:44,092
Crossing a river or other border

435
00:19:44,174 --> 00:19:46,966
acts that symbolize
crossing over to the afterlife

436
00:19:47,050 --> 00:19:49,383
these carry important
meanings in sorcery.

437
00:19:57,633 --> 00:20:02,925
(monster chittering, warbling)

438
00:20:03,008 --> 00:20:04,174
There it is.

439
00:20:06,299 --> 00:20:07,549
I'm looking forward to this.

440
00:20:07,633 --> 00:20:10,466
(monster warbling)

441
00:20:21,717 --> 00:20:22,634
Huh?

442
00:20:22,717 --> 00:20:24,175
What's this?

443
00:20:24,258 --> 00:20:26,134
Someone beat me here?

444
00:20:26,217 --> 00:20:27,051
Huh?

445
00:20:27,134 --> 00:20:29,967
Fushiguro, this
one's different, huh?

446
00:20:30,051 --> 00:20:31,051
Yeah.

447
00:20:31,550 --> 00:20:34,842
Then why don't you two
focus on that first one.

448
00:20:36,842 --> 00:20:39,258
I'll exorcise this one.

449
00:20:39,342 --> 00:20:40,592
Is that so?

450
00:20:40,675 --> 00:20:44,175
You're going to play
with me now, are you?

451
00:20:45,675 --> 00:20:48,760
(ending theme music)

452
00:22:16,178 --> 00:22:18,303
[Unison] Juju Stroll!

453
00:22:18,387 --> 00:22:19,387
Help, stop that guy!

454
00:22:19,470 --> 00:22:21,387
-He stole my purse!
-Huh?

455
00:22:26,179 --> 00:22:27,097
Thanks!

456
00:22:27,179 --> 00:22:28,721
This was so kind of you!

457
00:22:28,805 --> 00:22:30,930
Allow me to treat
you to a free meal.

458
00:22:31,013 --> 00:22:31,596
[Kugisaki] Oh we
couldn't accept that.

459
00:22:31,679 --> 00:22:33,471
[Itadori] Of course we could!

460
00:22:33,554 --> 00:22:34,594
Thank you! I'd love to eat!

461
00:22:36,805 --> 00:22:38,679
This restaurant has
been in my family

462
00:22:38,763 --> 00:22:40,721
for four generations now.

463
00:22:40,805 --> 00:22:43,721
That was supposed to come
to an end with my father.

464
00:22:43,805 --> 00:22:44,805
But I stayed.

465
00:22:44,846 --> 00:22:47,304
I insisted on trying to
keep it up and running.

466
00:22:48,471 --> 00:22:50,138
I just wanted to
keep the restaurant,

467
00:22:50,221 --> 00:22:51,741
and our special
style of cooking alive.

468
00:22:53,638 --> 00:22:55,972
[Both] Ahhh! What a nice story!

469
00:22:56,847 --> 00:22:59,514
[Woman] Sorry for the
wait! Here's our pride and joy,

470
00:22:59,597 --> 00:23:01,972
the gyoza meal passed
down for generations!

471
00:23:02,056 --> 00:23:03,222
[Unison] Let's dig in!

472
00:23:03,847 --> 00:23:05,806
Thank you for the meal!

473
00:23:11,722 --> 00:23:13,597
So, guys.

474
00:23:13,680 --> 00:23:14,823
Is it really gyoza
when there's no meat?

475
00:23:14,847 --> 00:23:18,305
Basically just cabbage
and some thickener?

476
00:23:18,389 --> 00:23:20,222
I'm so glad you said that!

477
00:23:20,305 --> 00:23:21,389
Yeah, right!

478
00:23:21,472 --> 00:23:24,472
And she was a really nice
woman and all that but come on!

479
00:23:24,555 --> 00:23:26,573
But apparently, gyoza is
meant to be a vegetable dish,

480
00:23:26,597 --> 00:23:29,223
not a meat dish.

481
00:23:29,306 --> 00:23:30,306
[Unison] Seriously?

482
00:23:30,390 --> 00:23:33,932
(upbeat instrumental music)

483
00:23:37,057 --> 00:23:40,057
"Episode 23: The Origin
of Blind Obedience - 2 -"

